# The new-tab page: a new tab opens on a page of the shell's own — a clock,
# a greeting by the hour and the date, over a gradient of the theme's
# colors when the theme names no pictures — with the address bar empty and
# focused, so typing goes straight to it. The replay's local time is fixed
# at a Monday morning, so the page is the same on every machine, and its
# clock ticks on the page's timers, which the virtual clock drives.
resize 800 500
key ctrl+t
assert-tabs 2
assert-focus address
assert-address
assert-title New Tab
assert-text 09:41
assert-text Good morning
assert-text Monday, 5 January
assert-golden goldens/newtab.png
advance 39000
assert-text 09:41
advance 1000
assert-text 09:42
assert-no-text 09:41

# The page by its address, and back to it: the time is the time now.
open about:newtab
assert-address
assert-title New Tab
assert-text 09:41
open data:text/html,<title>Elsewhere</title><p>Away
assert-title Elsewhere
back
assert-title New Tab
assert-text Good morning
